{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/488397-too-many-conspiracies-not-enough-compacts","id":488397,"title":"Too Many Conspiracies, Not Enough Compacts?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-22T10:02:20-07:00","id":488397,"title":"Too Many Conspiracies, Not Enough Compacts?","content":"So you all know I love me some fan-made hunter groups, but lately I've notice the trend focusing solely on conspiracies. I understand the appeal of conspiracies, but I'm wondering why so many of the community are focused away from new compacts? Is it the endowments conspiracies get to use, or is it just that conspiracies are cooler to customize?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T10:36:00-07:00","id":488465,"title":"","content":"It's the Endowments. At least, it is to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T18:30:30-07:00","id":488911,"title":"","content":"Well that, conspiracies also give you more bang for your buck.<br /> <br /> For the same amount of effort, you can build a global conspiracy that can support games all across the world and plenty of NPCs, or you can build a small organization not nearly as accomodating. <br /> <br /> By the core book, compacts have 50 to 200 people.<br /> <br /> So if you divided up every union member across the united states of america, there's four per state, at best. At that level of support, you're basically playing a tier 1 hunter game. <br /> <br /> If you make them more local, say having the union being found in the 10 states with the strongest unions: New York, Alaska, Hawaii, Washington, Michigan, Rhode Island, California, Oregon, Connecticut, and Illonois, that means the Union doesn't do you much good if you wanted a game about hunting chupucabra in Texas. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T01:21:24-07:00","id":489147,"title":"","content":"for me, it is both the scale and the power level. Endowments make hunters feel more then just humans with an axe and a flashlight- not that there is nothing wrong with this- this is what in hunter is about by the essence after all. However, it makes compacts into being kinda... weird. They lack the reach and resources of the conspiracies, making them limited to a certain place (maybe a city, a country at best), but they are also a bit more then just a cell- they have a pre- existing agenda, a real ideology and goals they seek to accomplish that goes beyond the current members of the compact. They feel like they were meant to have the best of the 3rd and 1st tiers, but in the end, for me, they feel like they are kinda lacking. They are 1st tier hunters who are not alone in the dark. They are 3rd tier hunters who don't have the cool guns.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying they don't have a place in hunter, just that I prefer seeing them as more of a &quot;design by yourself&quot; system then as a real splat. Maybe having compacts being either &quot;evolved cells&quot; or conspiracy &quot;sub divisions&quot; would have made them more interesting IMO- but personally, if I want an hunter org I want them with guns- not torches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T11:29:12-07:00","id":489678,"title":"","content":"You guys can speak for yourselves <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I've written a fairly even number of Conspiracies/Compacts.<br /> <br /> More to the point. I'd strongly reccomend people be open to the possibility of a Compact with a Conspiracy sized Endowment. (Which is to say a small decentralised organisation with mojo)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 04-23-2015, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T21:01:52-07:00","id":491238,"title":"","content":"I agree that the lean towards custom Conspiracies is mainly due to being able to design a custom Endowment to go with it. Personally, I've all but decoupled Compacts and Conspiracies from tiers. A Conspiracy can still operate at a cloistered local level, and Compacts can have Endowments of their own even if they don't have black helicopters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T23:15:55-07:00","id":491401,"title":"","content":"Go in the opposite direction. A Conpsiracy doesn't need an Endowment and a Compact can have one.<br /> <br /> You don't need a special keyword-beginning-with-C to say if they have an Endowment. An Endowment does that by itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T03:13:24-07:00","id":492476,"title":"","content":"I've always seen the connection as basically social darwinism in action- a compact with access to an endowment can survive longer and recruit more, allowing it to grow.<br /> <br /> Like the promethean brotherhood who have an endowment without becoming a conspiracy yet.<br /> <br /> Of course with compacts and conspiracies which gives the major compacts endowments, the mechanical difference is nonexistent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T09:55:23-07:00","id":494971,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but that's a trend not a rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T05:27:21-07:00","id":496193,"title":"","content":"Is the intent of the design that you actually use all within one game? I always saw the list as a list of suggestions with the idea that you would drop at least some of them...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T05:45:43-07:00","id":496202,"title":"","content":"The worlds a big place. You can probably assume they all exist without actually running into more than a handful in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T04:45:11-07:00","id":497319,"title":"","content":"You are free to have single conspiracy or compact hunter games of course, but there's an easy enough explanation for more varied groups than that- Hunters are rare.<br /> <br /> Average for a conspiracy, who are the big guns here in the hunter world, is only 1000 operatives, and conspiracies by definition are supposed to be global.<br /> <br /> If you have a game in which each hunter can protect 7 million people at a time all by themselves I think it's safe to say that you're playing a non standard hunter game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So what is a hunter going to do when they have a situation they don't have the resources to deal with it within their own group? Rush in and get themselves killed? Let innocents die and let the monster just whistle a jaunty tune as it goes on with whatever nefarious doings? Or make a call to those other hunters they've encountered?<br /> <br /> And if you prefer single conspiracy or compact games, well again, hunters are rare.<br /> <br /> There are undoubtedly countries with populations far in excess of 1000 people that I've not met a single representative from, and I doubt that ashwood abbey and union members go to the same parties.<br /> <br /> Also, a hunter can belong to more than one group at a time, although some are weirder combinations than others. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 04-30-2015, 07:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T10:25:32-07:00","id":497619,"title":"","content":"I think the 1000 operatives is a terrible idea though. A theme of Hunter is that numbers are strength - it's why the devs referred to Hunter as the Power Stat. Personally I think they should have either left numbers our or gone deep into detail on how the Conspiracy functions.<br /> <br /> (Also the Ascending Ones are far bigger than TF:V. They have to be given that they're three different Conspiracies and they have a whole &quot;common man&quot; thing going.)<br /> <br /> That said I agree that the list of Compacts and Conspiracies is a list of suggestions. You take some that will be in your game, some that exist but are elsewhere, drop others, add your own. I do prefer all PCs coming from the same org though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T02:08:12-07:00","id":498508,"title":"","content":"Numbers is strength fine, but strength isn't supposed to be on the hunter's side. They're supposed to be the scrappy underdog, not the empire from star wars.<br /> <br /> And conspiracies are supposed to be secret, the existence of the supernatural is an open secret, but if there are hundreds of thousands of hunters wondering around, that's just not a secret at all. <br /> <br /> That being said, if you want to buff up the membership of hunter groups, that's fine, but when you get to the point where there really should be hunter american pride parades you've probably gone too far. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T15:35:22-07:00","id":499453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/488397-too-many-conspiracies-not-enough-compacts?p=498508#post498508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Numbers is strength fine, but strength isn't supposed to be on the hunter's side. They're supposed to be the scrappy underdog, not the empire from star wars.</div> </div> </div> </div> On the contuary. That's practically a direct quote from a now sadly lost blog by the authors. Hunter was explicitly the &quot;Power Splat&quot; (Vampire - Soical, Werewolf - Physical, Mage - Mental, Promethian - Resistance, Changeling - Finease, Hunter - Power).<br /> <br /> Besides, there's three Tiers; the entire point of having different Tiers is to change how the game plays. Tier 1 is scrappy underdogs; so by nessessity Tier 2 and 3 aren't. Not that I would ever call anyone with WMDs underdogs. (TF:V has an anti-spirt nuke. AKD is said to have multiple WMD level weapons, the example being able to destory entire cities with an Earthquake. How many Moros would that take?)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/488397-too-many-conspiracies-not-enough-compacts?p=498508#post498508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And conspiracies are supposed to be secret, the existence of the supernatural is an open secret, but if there are hundreds of thousands of hunters wondering around, that's just not a secret at all.</div> </div> </div> </div> Eh; it's hardly more unrealisitc than the rest of the WoD.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T03:05:22-07:00","id":500072,"title":"","content":"Well i guess it all depends on how the theme of the games go. With compacts, i would assume there wouldn't be as many people lasting than joining. Some are just joining the hunt with conviction, a sawed-off and half an idea of what their doing. Under-doging can be fun but the Conspiracies with their endowments just feels like you can be more successful while being stylish with it. It doesn't have to be that way, mind you. But it 's to tempting not to ignore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>&quot;I am a daydreamer and a Night thinker.&quot;~</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1820-nightout","name":"Nightout","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T23:16:25-07:00","id":506425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/488397-too-many-conspiracies-not-enough-compacts?p=499453#post499453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> On the contuary. That's practically a direct quote from a now sadly lost blog by the authors. Hunter was explicitly the &quot;Power Splat&quot; (Vampire - Soical, Werewolf - Physical, Mage - Mental, Promethian - Resistance, Changeling - Finease, Hunter - Power).<br /> <br /> Besides, there's three Tiers; the entire point of having different Tiers is to change how the game plays. Tier 1 is scrappy underdogs; so by nessessity Tier 2 and 3 aren't. Not that I would ever call anyone with WMDs underdogs. (TF:V has an anti-spirt nuke. AKD is said to have multiple WMD level weapons, the example being able to destory entire cities with an Earthquake. How many Moros would that take?)</div> </div> </div> </div>One moros with enough matter to make a nuclear bomb. Or a mage with enough spirit to summon an earthquake spirit.<br /> <br /> For that matter, in the vampire chroniclers guide there's a scenario in which the vampire's city is being destroyed by a single vampire with a devotion making his zombies infectious.<br /> <br /> So let's see, two groups with WMDs, versus more than two groups that can include hundreds if not thousands of individuals who can wreck cities all by themselves.<br /> <br /> How is being outgunned and outclassed a position of power again?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}